    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 609,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "1972 FA Charity Shield\nThe 1972 FA Charity Shield was contested between Manchester City and Aston Villa . Normally , the Charity Shield would have been contested by the First Division champions and FA Cup holders , who were Derby County and Leeds United , but both declined the chance to play in the Charity Shield . Instead , Manchester City , who had finished in fourth place in the First Division ; and Aston Villa , who finished as Third Division champions accepted the invitation to play . The match was played at Villa Park and Manchester City won 1 -- 0 , following a penalty from striker Francis Lee ."
     }
